       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well above the maximum daily dose and puts the patient at real risk of acute liver injury. You also didn't give a clinical rationale, and I can't think of an indication that would justify it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more analgesia than that, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead, such as an NSAID or another non-acetaminophen agent. Tell me which drug and dose you'd like.\n\nIf you still want the dose as written, it should go through your pharmacy's high-dose override or direct order-entry process, with pharmacist review. I shouldn't enter it as a routine order."
